    "display_name": "Chlorine Levels",
    "long_instructions": "You are trying to determine whether splitting water samples based on whether their chlorine levels are over 4 mg/L will be effective at classifying water sample risk. To do this, you want to calculate the impurity of the group of water samples with high chlorine levels.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. Count how many samples are high risk when `chlorine` is greater than 4. Store that value in a variable called `high_risk`.\r\n2. Count how many samples are low risk when `chlorine` is greater than 4. Store that value in a variable  called `low_risk`.\r\n3. Calculate the impurity of the group. Remember that impurity can be computed by taking 1 and subtracting the squares of the proportions of each group (high risk and low risk).\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\n`samples` is a list of dictionaries. You might find it helpful to write a loop that iterates over the list and checks the values in each dictionary.\r\n\r\nYou can square a value using `x**2`:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nx**2\r\n```",
